@startuml
title Sequence Diagram(Login And Role Guard)
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant "Login Page" as Login
participant "Auth Store" as Store
participant "Route Guard" as Guard
participant "AuthController" as AC
participant "AuthService" as AS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

User -> Login : Enter username and password
Login -> AC : POST /auth/login
activate AC
AC -> AS : authenticate(username, password)
activate AS
AS -> DB : select User by username
DB --> AS : user row
AS -> AS : verify the password hash
AS -> AS : reject when the account is disabled
AS --> AC : token and roles
deactivate AS
AC --> Login : 200 OK
deactivate AC
Login -> Store : save the token and roles
Store --> Login : saved
Login --> User : Redirect by role

User -> Guard : Navigate to a page
activate Guard
Guard -> Store : read the token and roles
activate Store
Store --> Guard : token and roles
deactivate Store
alt there is no token
  Guard --> User : redirect to /login
else the role is not permitted
  Guard --> User : redirect to /403
else permitted
  Guard --> User : allow the route
end
deactivate Guard

note over Guard
  Resident lands on /my-parcels.
  Staff, Owner and Administrator land on /dashboard.
  An API 401 clears the store and returns to /login.
end note

note over AC
  One endpoint serves all four roles.
  The role decides the landing page, not the login form.
end note
@enduml